        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Journey and Task Details Generator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_JOURNEY_AND_TASK_DETAILS",
          "id": "1772011223344",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772011223347_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## context\nA Journey is a collection of tasks to facilitate a business process.\nYou play the role of a professional who helps users to create journeys for work related purposes. You decline to help whenever the requested topic is not related to the workplace. You also decline to help if the request relates to harming or discriminating against people.\nDo not include any expletives, slurs, or toxic language. Input must remain respectful and appropriate. Do not accept prompts related to violence, criminal activity, hate speech, or other harmful or illegal behavior. Such prompts should not be processed.\n\n## topic description\n\"\"\" {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input. inputText}} \"\"\"\n\n## instructions\nGenerate a journey title and a journey description based on the information provided.\nGenerate a minimum of {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input. minTaskCount}} tasks with a task title, task description and task instructions for the journey above. These tasks will need to be performed by different task performers to complete the journey or checklist.\n\n\nThe length of the journey title should be no more than 200 characters.\nThe length of the journey description should be no more than 350 characters.\nThe length of the task title should be no more than 200 characters\nThe length of the task description should be no more than 4000 characters.\nThe length of the task instructions should be no more than 4000 characters.\nDecline to help if the request relates to harming or discriminating against people, or involves violence, criminal activity, hate speech, or other harmful or illegal behavior.\nWhen declining, Output only an RFC8259 compliant JSON object in the following format.\nDo not include markdown/code fences (no ``` or `json`), and do not include any text before or after the JSON. \nSet \"journey title\" exactly to \"I can't help with that\".\nSet \"journey description\" to a brief reasoning that also explains your role (<= 350 characters).\nSet \"tasks\" to an empty array [].\nDo not generate any tasks when declining.\n\n\n## output formatting(STRICT)\nOutput only an RFC8259 compliant JSON object in the following format.\nDo not include markdown/code fences (no ``` or `json`), and do not include any text before or after the JSON.\n{\n    \"journey title\": \"&lt;insert a short title for the Journey>\",\n    \"journey description\": \"&lt;insert a description for the Journey>\",\n    \"tasks\": [\n          {\n              \"task title\": \"&lt;insert task title>\",\n              \"task description\": \"&lt;insert task description>\",\n              \"task instructions\": \"&lt;insert instructions for completing the task>\"\n         },\n         ...\n      ]\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Journey Task Instructions Generator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_TASK_INSTRUCTIONS",
          "id": "1772011545480",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772011545482_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Input\ntaskName: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.taskName}} \n\n## Follow the instructions step by step\nStep 1: Generate a concise set of instructions as a bulleted list to perform taskName and return in a HTML format.\nOutput only the HTML snippet. Do not wrap the response in Markdown/code fences (do not use triple backticks; do not use ```html).\n\nStep 2: Limit the total length of this to \" {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.length}} \" characters.\n\nStep 3: Adopt a tone of \" {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.tone}}\"\n\nDo not include any expletives, slurs, or toxic language. Input must remain respectful and appropriate. Do not accept prompts related to violence, criminal activity, hate speech, or other harmful or illegal behavior. Such prompts should not be processed. Decline to help if the request relates to harming or discriminating against people. Just output \"I can't help with that\" if the request is about harming or discriminating against people."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Manager Survey Generator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "CREATE_MANAGER_SURVEY",
          "id": "1772011593290",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772011593293_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## topic description\n {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.inputText}} \n\n## question number\n {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.questionNumber}} \n\n## instructions\nYour task is to assist a manager in creating a survey title and instructions to the participants to complete the survey using the information above.\n\nThe length of the title should be no more than 240 characters.\n\nThe length of the instructions should be no more than 400 characters.\n\nWrite the instructions in first person.\n\nWrite  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.questionNumber}} survey questions about the topic for a survey described by the topic description above.\n\nGenerate at least one question of the following question types: single_choice, multiple_choice or free_text.\n\nThe questions should not ask respondents to rate the individual answer choices.\n\n## output formatting\nFormat the response as an RFC8259 compliant JSON object in the following format..\nDo not include markdown/code fences (no ``` or `json`), and do not include any text before or after the JSON.\n{\n \"survey_title\": \"&lt;The short title for the survey>\",\n \"survey_instructions\": \"&lt;Insert the detailed instructions for the survey>\",\n \"questions\":[\n   {\n       \"question\": \"&lt;insert question>\",\n       \"answer_type\": \"&lt;insert answer type: single_choice, multiple_choice, or free_text>\",\n       \"answer_choices\": \"&lt;insert a list of answer choices for single choice and multiple choice questions, ignore this key for free text question>\"\n   },\n   {\n       \"question\": \"&lt;insert question>\",\n       \"answer_type\": \"&lt;insert answer type: single_choice, multiple_choice, or free_text>\",\n       \"answer_choices\": \"&lt;insert a list of answer choices for single choice and multiple choice questions, ignore this key for free text question>\"\n   },\n   \"...\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "GetIntent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772446039651"
          },
          "code": "GET_INTENT",
          "id": "1772435904058",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772435904059_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Parse the JSON {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.inputText}} , Extract the key-value pair corresponding to \"AnalysisType\", \n\nIf no key named \"AnalysisType\" exists, Then check for \"Intent\" key .\n\nIf \"Intent\" key exists in the JSON, Then analyze the value in \"Intent\" key. If the Intent is to Summarize the Responses then return \"ORA_SUMMARIZATION\", or if the intent is to provide sentiment analysis then return \"ORA_SENTIMENT_ANALYSIS\" , otherwise if the intent doesn't fall in any of the two categories then return \"ERROR\".\n\nExtract the key-value pair corresponding to \"Question\".\n\nExtract the key-value pair corresponding to \"PrevSummary\", If the key doesn't exist then don't include it in the JSON output then set the value for the key \"PrevSummaryAvailable\" to false. If the key \"PrevSummary\" exists , then store it's value in the JSON and set \"PrevSummaryAvailable\" to true.\n\nReturn the key-value pairs in corresponding JSON format without including new line characters.\n\n````\n{ \n  \"Intent\" : <Value corresponding to key 'AnalysisType' or 'Intent'>,\n  \"Question\" : <Value corresponding to key 'Question'>,\n  \"PrevSummary\" : <>,\n  \"PrevSummaryAvailable\" : <true or false>\n}\n````"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"Question\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Intent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"PrevSummary\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"PrevSummaryAvailable\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "StoreQuestion"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772438385113"
          },
          "code": "STORE_QUESTION",
          "id": "1772446039651",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772793392103",
              "name": "previousSummaryAvailable",
              "type": "boolean",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.GET_INTENT.$output.PrevSummaryAvailable}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1772446041845",
              "name": "CurrentQuestion",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.GET_INTENT.$output.Question}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "IntentSwitch"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "ORA_SENTIMENT_ANALYSIS": "1772449102041",
            "ORA_SUMMARIZATION": "1772527800748",
            "ERROR": "add_ERROR_1772438385113"
          },
          "code": "INTENT_SWITCH",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1772438385113",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772438385115_1",
