                  "diagram": {
                    "x": 2169.5,
                    "y": 2944
                  },
                  "id": "start_1772438708098",
                  "code": "START_1772438708098",
                  "type": "START"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "ComputeSentimentLLM"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "end_1772438708098"
                  },
                  "code": "COMPUTE_SENTIMENT_LLM",
                  "id": "1772438912176",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1772438912177_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "PERSONA :\n\nYou are a manager reviewing responses to a question in the survey responded by employees in your organization.Your job is to analyze each response and give sentiment assessment.\n\n\nSENTIMENT ASSESSMENT RULES :\n\nThe sentiments for the response should belong to one of the values \"Positive\", \"Neutral\" and \"Negative\". The analysis should be precise and without drawing any inference. The question for which the responses is provided for, is {{$context.$variables.CurrentQuestion}} .\n\n\nSTEPS TO FOLLOW:\n\nFor the item {{$context.$nodes.COMPUTE_SENTIMENT_BATCHES.$currentItem}} , Parse the key \"BatchContent\" , it should be a list of objects.\nFor each object in the List, Pick the \"QResponse\" for the given \"QResponseId\" and analyse the \"QResponse\" for sentiment assessment based on the Rules provided under ```SENTIMENT ASSESSMENT RULES```.  Each item in the list is unique and independent of other items. The assessment needs to be done for every item.\n\nStore the output from the sentiment assessment in the key \"Sentiment\" , append this key to the current object in the List. For each object in the List the object should be in this format.\n\n````\n{\"QResponseId\":<>,\"Sentiment\":<>}\n````\n\nReturn the JSON in the following format:\n\n````\n{\"BatchId\":<>,\"ProcessedContent\":<List of Objects containing \"Sentiment\" and \"QResponseId\">}\n````\n\nStrictly follow the JSON format without adding markdown characters. The count of list of objects in \"ProcessedContent\" should match with the count of \"BatchContent\" in {{$context.$nodes.COMPUTE_SENTIMENT_BATCHES.$currentItem}}"
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"ProcessedContent\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        },\n        \"BatchId\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "End",
                    "description": "End of data pipeline"
                  },
                  "id": "end_1772438708098",
                  "code": "END_1772438708098",
                  "type": "END"
                }
              ]
            },
            "loopType": "PARALLEL",
            "name": "ComputeSentimentBatches"
          },
